Not a real file to add as-is — this is a diff note for
toolkit/components/extensions/MatchPattern.cpp (a large stock Mozilla file;
only one atom set entry is added).

See the companion diff note at
gecko/patches/pyxis/xpcom/ds/StaticAtoms.py.PYXIS_DIFF for the full
root-cause writeup. This half of the fix: add the new `nsGkAtoms::pyxis`
atom (added there) to the `HostLocatorSchemes()` static atom set here, so
MatchPatternCore recognizes "pyxis://host/path" as using host-locator syntax
instead of falling into the "unrecognized scheme, match path literally"
branch that silently broke `matches: ["pyxis://*/*"]`.

Real excerpt (search for `DEFINE_STATIC_ATOM_SET(HostLocatorSchemes` — near
the top of the file, around the other atom-set definitions):

    // Known schemes that are followed by "://" instead of ":".
    DEFINE_STATIC_ATOM_SET(HostLocatorSchemes, nsGkAtoms::http, nsGkAtoms::https,
                           nsGkAtoms::ws, nsGkAtoms::wss, nsGkAtoms::file,
                           nsGkAtoms::ftp, nsGkAtoms::moz_extension,
                           nsGkAtoms::chrome, nsGkAtoms::resource, nsGkAtoms::moz,
                           nsGkAtoms::moz_icon, nsGkAtoms::moz_gio,
                           nsGkAtoms::pyxis);

(just `nsGkAtoms::pyxis` appended to the existing argument list.)

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
The unified diff below is generated from the checkout and is applied with
  git apply gecko/patches/pyxis/<path>.PYXIS_DIFF
(or `patch -p1 <`). Everything above this line is rationale, not content;
git apply ignores it. Regenerate with scripts/regen-gecko-patches.sh.
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

diff --git a/toolkit/components/extensions/MatchPattern.cpp b/toolkit/components/extensions/MatchPattern.cpp
index 2c028dd624aa..4ac961cc3b72 100644
--- a/toolkit/components/extensions/MatchPattern.cpp
+++ b/toolkit/components/extensions/MatchPattern.cpp
@@ -87,11 +87,15 @@ DEFINE_STATIC_ATOM_SET(PermittedSchemes, nsGkAtoms::http, nsGkAtoms::https,
                        nsGkAtoms::ftp, nsGkAtoms::data);
 
 // Known schemes that are followed by "://" instead of ":".
+// nsGkAtoms::pyxis: Pyxis's custom app-serving scheme (see StaticAtoms.py's
+// comment on that atom for the real bug this fixes — without it here,
+// JSWindowActor `matches: ["pyxis://*/*"]` patterns silently never matched).
 DEFINE_STATIC_ATOM_SET(HostLocatorSchemes, nsGkAtoms::http, nsGkAtoms::https,
                        nsGkAtoms::ws, nsGkAtoms::wss, nsGkAtoms::file,
                        nsGkAtoms::ftp, nsGkAtoms::moz_extension,
                        nsGkAtoms::chrome, nsGkAtoms::resource, nsGkAtoms::moz,
-                       nsGkAtoms::moz_icon, nsGkAtoms::moz_gio);
+                       nsGkAtoms::moz_icon, nsGkAtoms::moz_gio,
+                       nsGkAtoms::pyxis);
 
 DEFINE_STATIC_ATOM_SET(WildcardSchemes, nsGkAtoms::http, nsGkAtoms::https,
                        nsGkAtoms::ws, nsGkAtoms::wss);
